                          "index":  0,
                          "text":  "I was fine, though. And I had something no Surveyor before me had: an arm with a scoop. People on Earth sent commands and I dug four little trenches, pressed on the soil, and even dropped some on my own footpad so my camera could take a look. We learned the ground was firm, a bit like damp sand. Firm enough for astronauts.\n\nTwo weeks after I landed, the Sun set. Night on the Moon lasts about two weeks and gets terribly cold. I never woke up.",
